    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28556" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύη</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ἡ,</span>
		
			Dor.
		 (not in Trag.) <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύα</span></b> ,
		poet. Noun, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>misery, anguish,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.215
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῆμα δύης</span> height
				<i>of woe,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				338
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέλαγος ἀτηρᾶς δύης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					746
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενναία δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					938
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πημοναῖς δύαις τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					513
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				181
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				525
			</span></i>, etc.: also in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				4.42
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				Pythag.
			</span></i> name for <i>two</i> (by false etym.),
				<i>Theol,Ar.</i><i><span class="en">
				12
			</span></i>.</div>
